Plans for V1:
Pretty much a 1:1 copy of the simple Excel assignment. I want a 1D simulator (No parachute) that tracks time, mass (all mks), Altitude, Velocity, Acceleration, Net force, Weight, Thrust, Drag
Time: 0.1 seconds timestep
Mass: in Kg, will be changing due to loss of fuel mass (averaged fuel loss subtracted over time)
Altitude: in Meters and found with y=vt+(1/2)at^2 Edit: decided to use y=vt due to the defiction of v=dy/dt.
Velocity: Meters/Second found through v=at
Acceleration: Meters/Second^2 found theough F=ma
Force: Newtons and sum of forces.
Weight: Mass*Gravity (9.81m/s^2)
Thrust: Averaged thrust found with ThrustCurve.org
Drag: Newtons and found using D= 1/2*Cd*A*p*V^2. The drag coefficient will be from standard models. Density will be 1.225 kg/m^3 (ISA Density at sea level), have area be simple circle area for rocket-tube
Inputs:
Initial Dry Mass, Rocket Radius, Thrust data, massloss data

